{"name":"Minimalist","hex":"#cabead","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"minimalist","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Believing in or seeking a minimal state; seeking to minimize or reduce to a minimum."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One who believes in or seeks a minimal state; one who seeks to minimize or reduce to a minimum."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/minimalist"}],"entries":[{"title":"Minimalism","blocks":[{"text":"Minimalism is an art movement that emphasizes reducing art to its essentials, focusing on the object itself and the viewer's experience, with as little mediation from the artist as possible. It emerged in the post-World War II era in Western art, and is often interpreted as a reaction to abstract expressionism and modernism."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Donald%D6%B9Judd_IMJ.JPG/330px-Donald%D6%B9Judd_IMJ.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Minimalism","wikidata":"Q173436"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/SANAA%2C_Zollverein_School_of_Management_and_Design%2C_Essen_%284606034520%29.jpg/500px-SANAA%2C_Zollverein_School_of_Management_and_Design%2C_Essen_%284606034520%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/SANAA%2C_Zollverein_School_of_Management_and_Design%2C_Essen_%284606034520%29.jpg/500px-SANAA%2C_Zollverein_School_of_Management_and_Design%2C_Essen_%284606034520%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASANAA%2C_Zollverein_School_of_Management_and_Design%2C_Essen_(4606034520).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Kazimir_Malevich%2C_1915%2C_Black_Suprematic_Square%2C_oil_on_linen_canvas%2C_79.5_x_79.5_